.TH LOOM 1 "October 2026" "loom 0.9.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
loom \- unified agentic ecosystem for sharing skills, sessions, and MCP servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loom
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loom
is a single CLI front\-end for an ecosystem of agentic coding tools.
It ships preset adapters for twelve agent tools:
.BR jcode ,
.BR crush ,
.BR claude\-code ,
.BR opencode ,
.BR goose ,
.BR codex ,
.BR cursor ,
.BR gemini\-cli ,
.BR aider ,
.BR kiro ,
.BR juno ,
and
.BR github\-copilot .
.PP
It manages a shared directory at
.BR ~/.loom/
that contains discovered skills, MCP server configurations, session
exports, authentication credentials, hooks, and a knowledge graph, so
that the same context is available to every tool the developer
launches.
.PP
A background daemon,
.BR loomd (1),
aggregates the per\-crate subsystems and exposes them over a Unix
domain socket at
.BR ~/.loom/loomd.sock ;
the CLI connects to the daemon when one is running, or runs a small
subset of operations standalone.  The daemon is auto\-started on
demand and shuts itself down after 5 minutes of idle IPC traffic.
Loom targets Unix\-like systems (Linux/macOS); on Windows it requires
WSL2 \(em native Windows is not supported, because the daemon relies
on Unix domain sockets.
.PP
Model routing scores each task's complexity and routes it to one of
three tiers
.RI ( Slm ", Mid, " Flagship ")"
mapped onto concrete provider/model pairs from a configurable
catalog.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Lifecycle
.TP
.B init
Initialize the
.B ~/.loom/
ecosystem directory.  Accepts
.B \-\-import
(short
.BR \-i )
to scan the local filesystem and build the initial snapshot,
.B \-\-recommended
(short
.BR \-r )
to install the recommended set of MCP servers (filesystem, github,
playwright, agentmemory), and
.B \-\-source \fIURL\fR
to bootstrap from a remote config (HTTPS only); the URL is written to
.B config.toml
as
.B remote_config_url
and the content is fetched and cached immediately, so subsequent
.B loom
commands deep\-merge the cached remote config on top of the local
tree.
.TP
.B scan \fR[\-\-json]
Print a summary of the resources currently registered with the
ecosystem.
.TP
.B status \fR[\-\-json]
Show ecosystem and daemon health.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\-\-json] [\-\-fix] [\-\-verbose]
Run deep diagnostics for the daemon, service installation, and
persistence layer.
.B \-\-fix
(short
.BR \-f )
creates missing directories and initializes missing files;
.B \-\-verbose
(short
.BR \-v )
prints explanations for each check.
.TP
.B tui
Launch the terminal UI dashboard (built when the
.B tui
cargo feature is enabled, which is the default).  The dashboard has
fifteen tabs: Dashboard, Daemon, Discovery, MCP, Skills, Sessions,
Logs, Knowledge, PRs, Runtime, Kanban, Graph, Cost, Orchestrator,
and Review.
.TP
.B self\-update \fR[\-\-force] [\-\-source \fISOURCE\fR]
Check for a newer version and install it.
.I SOURCE
is
.B github
(the default) or
.BR releases.loom.sh .
.B \-\-force
re\-downloads even when the versions match.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell completions for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
.BR powershell ,
or
.BR elvish .
.SS Config inspection
.TP
.B config show \fR[\-\-json] [\-\-extends] [\-\-no\-extend] [\-\-no\-remote]
Print the merged
.B LoomConfig
after applying all five precedence layers
.RI ( defaults
<\fIextends\fR
<\fIlocal config.toml\fR
<\fIlayer overlays\fR
<\fIremote cache\fR).
Accepts
.B \-\-json
for machine\-readable output and
.B \-\-extends
to print the resolved source chain (label, path, contributed keys for
each layer).
.B \-\-no\-extend
and
.B \-\-no\-remote
skip the corresponding layer for a single command (env var
equivalents:
.BR LOOM_NO_EXTEND=1 ,
.BR LOOM_NO_REMOTE=1 ).
The
.B extends
chain is limited to a depth of 10 with cycle detection.
.TP
.B config validate \fR[\-\-no\-extend] [\-\-no\-remote]
Validate the merged
.B LoomConfig
without writing anything.  Same
.B \-\-no\-extend
and
.B \-\-no\-remote
flags as
.BR "config show" .
.TP
.B config fetch \fR[\-\-url \fIURL\fR]
Download the remote config (HTTPS only) to
.BR ~/.loom/.cache/remote_config/ ,
with SHA\-256 based caching.  If
.B \-\-url
is omitted, uses
.B remote_config_url
from the current
.BR config.toml .
.SS Tool and integration management
.TP
.B thread \fITOOL\fR \fR[\-\-apply\-routing \fIDECISION\fR]
Register or update an agentic tool.
.B \-\-apply\-routing
immediately adopts a routing decision into the tool environment.
.TP
.B exec \fITOOLS...\fR \fR[\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-parallel] [\-\-pool\-size \fIN\fR] [\-\-no\-isolation] [\-\- \fIARGS...\fR]
Execute agentic tool(s) with the Loom ecosystem loaded.  Sequential
mode (the default) enables the ecosystem for every named tool and
launches the last one, passing arguments after
.B \-\-
to it.  Parallel mode
.B (\-\-parallel)
runs all named tools concurrently with per\-task git worktree
isolation: each agent is launched in a detached\-HEAD worktree on a
.B loom\-parallel/<agent>\-<timestamp>
branch created next to the repository.
.B \-\-pool\-size
caps concurrency (default 4),
.B \-\-no\-isolation
skips worktree isolation in parallel mode, and
.B \-\-dry\-run
prints the injected environment without executing anything.
.TP
.B init\-shell \fR[\-\-shell bash|zsh|fish]
Generate shell integration that activates Loom on
.BR cd
(shell defaults to auto\-detection).
.TP
.B sync \fR[\-\-tool \fITOOL\fR] [\-\-json]
Sync Loom\-managed resources to tool\-native filesystem locations,
optionally limited to a single tool.
.TP
.B add\-acp\-agent \fIAGENT_ID\fR
Pull an agent entry from the public ACP registry
(cdn.agentclientprotocol.com) and add it locally.
.TP
.B lock \fR[\-\-generate] [\-\-verify] [\-\-diff]
Manage the skill lock file
.RB ( ~/.loom/skills/skills.lock )
used to pin skill versions for reproducibility.
.B \-\-generate
(short
.BR \-g )
writes the lock file from current registry state,
.B \-\-verify
(short
.BR \-V )
checks installed skills against it, and
.B \-\-diff
shows violations in diff style.
.TP
.B plugin \fIACTION\fR
Manage the plugin registry:
.B search
(query),
.B install
(name, URL of a tool TOML, optional
.B \-\-version
and
.B \-\-verify
for Ed25519 signature checking),
.B register
(from a local tool TOML file),
.BR update ,
.BR remove ,
.BR list ,
and
.BR show .
.TP
.B remote \fIACTION\fR
Manage remote SSH connections:
.B list ,
.B add
(name, host; options
.BR \-\-port ,
.BR \-\-user ,
.BR \-\-key ,
.BR \-\-store\-in\-vault ,
.BR \-\-vault\-password ,
.BR \-\-agent ,
.BR \-\-jump ),
.BR remove ,
.B exec
(run a command on a remote host;
.B \-\-capture\-session
stores the output as an indexed Loom session), and
.B sync
(push or pull files with rsync, or scp with
.BR \-\-scp ;
.B \-\-pull
reverses the direction).
.TP
.B lsp \fIACTION\fR
LSP integration:
.B servers
(list available language servers),
.B rename
.RB ( \-\-path ,
.BR \-\-line ,
.BR \-\-column ,
new name),
.B find\-references
.RB ( \-\-path ,
.BR \-\-symbol ),
and
.B exec
(run rename, find\-references, gotodef, code\-action, or symbols
through a registered tool adapter).  Each accepts
.B \-\-server
to override auto\-detection from the file extension.
.TP
.B debug \fIACTION\fR
Debug Adapter Protocol integration:
.B adapters
(list available debug adapters),
.B launch
.RB ( \-\-program ,
.BR \-\-language ,
optional
.BR \-\-args ),
.B attach
.RB ( \-\-pid ,
.BR \-\-language ),
.B breakpoints
.RB ( \-\-file ,
.BR \-\-line ,
active session required),
.B step
(over, in, or out),
.B evaluate
(expression),
.B stack
(current stack trace), and
.B continue
(attach to a session launched via
.B "debug launch"
and continue it).
.TP
.B edit \fIACTION\fR
Content\-hash anchored editing (Hashline):
.B hash
(compute the anchor for a line range),
.B apply
(replace the anchored region with new content;
.B \-\-write
writes, default is a dry run), and
.B validate
(check that an anchor still matches the file).  Lines are 1\-based.
.TP
.B ast \fIACTION\fR
AST structural editing with tree\-sitter.  Sixteen actions:
.BR parse ,
.BR query ,
.BR node\-at ,
.BR move\-up ,
.BR move\-down ,
.BR swap ,
.BR extract ,
.BR wrap ,
.BR unwrap ,
.BR duplicate ,
.BR insert ,
.BR replace ,
.BR kind\-at ,
.BR find\-kind ,
.BR format ,
and
.BR stats .
Positions are 0\-based
.BI line / column
pairs; most actions accept a
.B \-\-language
override (rust, python, javascript, go, json),
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
and/or
.BR \-\-json .
.B wrap
supports if, if_true, if_false, loop, while, block, parens,
brackets, try, try_catch, unsafe, or a custom wrapper containing
.BR $BODY .
.TP
.B conflict \fIACTION\fR
Detect and resolve merge conflicts:
.B scan
(a file or directory),
.B resolve
(one file; strategies
.BR ours ,
.BR theirs ,
.BR both\-ours\-theirs ,
.BR both\-theirs\-ours ;
.B \-\-write
writes, default prints),
.B resolve\-bulk
(multiple files, one strategy), and
.B show
(detailed conflict info).
.SS Subsystems
.TP
.B mcp \fIACTION\fR
Manage MCP servers:
.B list ,
.B show ,
.B add
(stub),
.BR remove ,
.B install
(a known npm\-based server;
.B \-\-prewarm
pre\-warms the npm cache),
.B install\-recommended
(all recommended servers),
.B list\-known
(installable servers), and
.B serve
(start the stdio\-based Loom MCP server for MCP\-compatible tools).
.TP
.B skills \fIACTION\fR
Manage skills:
.B list
.RB ( \-\-locked
verifies against the lock file),
.B show
(by name),
.B install
(from a file path), and
.B remove
(by name).  There is no
.B "skills add"
subcommand.
.TP
.B sessions \fIACTION\fR
Manage session exports.  Actions:
.BR list ,
.BR show ,
.BR export ,
.BR import ,
.BR resume ,
.BR search ,
.BR recall ,
.BR index ,
.BR branch ,
.BR tag ,
.BR tags ,
.BR summarize ,
and
.BR merge .
.B list
and
.B search
accept
.B \-\-tag
to filter to sessions whose tag set intersects the given tags
(repeatable, OR semantics).
.B export
writes a portable JSON bundle (default
.IR sessions/exports/{id}.loom.json ,
override with
.BR \-o/\-\-output );
.B import
reads one back.
.B resume
restarts a session interactively with an LLM provider
.RB ( \-\-provider ,
.BR \-\-model )
or launches an agent tool with the session context
.RB ( \-\-agent );
.B \-\-inject\-memory
and
.B \-\-inject\-knowledge
prepend cross\-session memory and knowledge\-graph entities.
.B recall
groups matching messages by session, returning the top sessions
(hit count + best match) for a query, while
.B search
returns individual messages (both FTS5).
.B branch
forks a session at a checkpoint
.RB ( \-\-from ,
.BR \-\-checkpoint ).
.B tag
mutates a session's tag set
.RB ( \-\-add /
.BR \-\-remove );
.B tags
lists every distinct tag in the index.
.B summarize
auto\-compresses a session once its message count exceeds the
compression threshold (default 20,
.IR SESSION_COMPRESSION_THRESHOLD ):
older messages are folded into a single System\-role summary at the
head of the message list, and the last 10 messages
.RI ( SESSION_FULL_FIDELITY_COUNT )
are kept verbatim; it auto\-runs when a session crosses the
threshold, and
.B \-\-force
re\-runs it even below the threshold.
.B merge
appends messages from one session into another.
.TP
.B auth \fIACTION\fR
Manage authentication providers and the encrypted credential vault:
.B list
(auth entries),
.B providers
(registered LLM providers),
.B show
(a provider's configuration), and
.B validate
(a provider's credential).
.TP
.B hooks \fIACTION\fR
Manage event hooks:
.BR list ,
.BR show ,
.B register
(from a file path),
.BR remove ,
.B run
.RB ( \-\-event ,
.BR \-\-tool ,
optional
.BR \-\-matcher ),
and
.B verify
(hook signatures).
Supported event types are
.B PreToolUse
(a non\-zero exit blocks the tool call),
.BR PostToolUse ,
.BR SessionStart ,
and
.B PostPhase
(fired after a workflow phase completes, with
.IR LOOM_TASK_ID ,
.IR LOOM_TASK_PHASE ,
.IR LOOM_AGENT ,
and
.IR LOOM_EXIT_CODE
set for the hook script).
.TP
.B workflow \fIACTION\fR
Manage workflow tasks:
.BR list ,
.BR show ,
.BR create ,
.BR remove ,
.BR draft\-plan ,
.BR advance ,
.BR assign ,
.BR dispatch ,
.BR set\-sub\-agents ,
and
.B template
.RB ( list / show / create / remove ).
.B create
accepts
.BR \-\-title ,
.BR \-\-description ,
.B \-\-from\-issue
.RI ( owner/repo#123 ),
.B \-\-from\-ticket
.RI ( github: ,
.BR linear: ,
.BR gitlab: ,
or
.BR jira: )
prefixes),
.BR \-\-repo ,
.BR \-\-token ,
.BR \-\-template ,
.B \-\-from\-plan
(chief plan JSON), and
.BR \-\-worktree /
.B \-\-no\-worktree
(a per\-task git worktree under
.B ~/.loom/worktrees/
is created by default).
.B draft\-plan
turns a goal plus free\-text details into task lines
.RB ( \-\-create
imports them as tasks).
.B advance
moves a task to its next phase
.RB ( \-\-update\-issue
posts a comment on the linked issue, with optional
.BR \-\-comment ).
.B assign
overrides the routed provider/model and sets the agent tool.
.B dispatch
sends the task to an agent tool (default: the task's last agent),
with
.BR \-\-link\-issue ,
.BR \-\-create\-branch ,
.B \-\-mode \fIsingle|sub\-agents\fR,
.B \-\-runtime \fIprocess|docker|podman|kubernetes\fR,
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
and extra tool arguments after
.BR \-\- .
With
.B \-\-auto\-advance
(sub\-agents mode) the daemon loops phase after phase: each agent
writes its result to
.IR ~/.loom/workflow/tasks/{task_id}.{phase}.result.json
(or
.BR .result.md ),
exposed via
.BR LOOM_EXPECTED_RESULT_PATH ;
the previous phase's result and sessions are injected via
.B LOOM_PRIOR_PHASE_RESULT
and
.BR LOOM_PRIOR_SESSIONS .
Every dispatch is captured as a session and indexed into memory and
the knowledge graph unless
.B \-\-no\-capture\-session
is given.
.B set\-sub\-agents
configures per\-phase agents
.RB ( \-\-plan ,
.BR \-\-implement ,
.BR \-\-verify ,
.BR \-\-finish )
with
.B \-\-max\-retries
(default 3) and
.BR \-\-fallback\-agent .
.TP
.B routing \fIACTION\fR
Inspect and override the complexity\-scoring model router:
.B show
(config and catalog),
.B evaluate
(score + decision for a prompt),
.B score
(complexity score only),
.B recommend
(for an existing task),
.B override
.RB ( \-\-tier \fIslm|mid|flagship\fR ,
optional
.BR \-\-reason ),
.B outcomes
(persisted decisions and their outcomes), and
.B catalog
.RB ( \-\-refresh ,
.BR \-\-json ).
.TP
.B runtime \fIACTION\fR
Runtime management:
.B list
(available runtimes),
.B set\-default
.RI ( process ,
.BR docker ),
and
.B status
(current default and health).
.TP
.B rules \fIACTION\fR
Event\-stream rules:
.BR list ,
.B show ,
.B add
.RB ( \-\-name ,
.BR \-\-event\-type ,
.BR \-\-field ,
.B \-\-operator \fIequals|neq|gt|lt|contains|starts-with|ends-with\fR,
.BR \-\-value ,
.BR \-\-action\-log ,
.BR \-\-action\-suppress ,
.BR \-\-priority ),
.BR remove ,
and
.B eval
(test a synthetic event against all rules).
.TP
.B knowledge \fIACTION\fR
Build and query the SQLite knowledge graph:
.B build
(from indexed sessions;
.B \-\-llm
switches to LLM\-based extraction),
.B query
(subgraph around an entity,
.B \-\-depth
default 2),
.BR stats ,
.B add
.RB ( \-\-entity\-type ,
.BR \-\-canonical ),
.B relate
(from, predicate, to,
.B \-\-weight
0.0\(en1.0),
.B search
(by name/type), and
.B clear
.RB ( \-\-force
required).
.TP
.B memory \fIACTION\fR
Manage the AgentMemory persistent memory server:
.B status ,
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.B retain
(store a durable fact;
.BR \-\-type ,
.BR \-\-source ,
.BR \-\-importance ),
.B recall
(search hindsight memory), and
.B reflect
(synthesize an overview for a question or topic).
.TP
.B issues \fIACTION\fR
Manage issue tracker integration:
.B list
.RB ( \-\-repo ,
.BR \-\-state ,
.BR \-\-labels ,
.BR \-\-token ,
.BR \-\-provider ,
.BR \-\-host ),
.B show ,
.B create\-branch
(branch from an issue),
.B link\-pr
(comment a PR URL on an issue),
.B pull\-requests
(GitHub only),
.B diff
(a PR's diff),
.B ci\-status
(a PR's CI state), and
.B create\-pr
(create via
.BR gh ).
Providers:
.B github
(default),
.BR linear ,
.BR jira ,
and
.B gitlab
.RB ( \-\-host
for Jira/GitLab instances;
.I GITHUB_TOKEN
is the default token source).
.TP
.B telemetry \fIACTION\fR
Telemetry metrics and counters:
.B show
.RB ( \-\-json )
and
.B reset
(both require a running daemon).
.SS Daemon
.TP
.B daemon \fIstart|stop|status|restart\fR
Manage the background
.BR loomd (1)
process.
.B start
spawns
.B loomd
with
.B LOOM_AGENTS_DIR
set and records its pid in
.BR ~/.loom/.cache/loomd.pid ;
.B status
accepts
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B daemon install\-service
Install
.B loomd
as a user\-level service (launchd on macOS, systemd on Linux).
.TP
.B daemon uninstall\-service
Remove the user service.
.TP
.B acp \fIACTION\fR
Manage the ACP dispatch server hosted by the daemon:
.B status ,
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.B show
(detailed info), and
.B agents
(list launchable agents).
.B acp run
runs one canonical ACP prompt turn against an agent program
directly:
.RS
.B loom acp run \fIPROGRAM\fR \-\-prompt \fITEXT\fR
.RB [ \-\-cwd \fIDIR\fR]
.RB [ \-\-timeout\-secs \fIN\fR]
.RB [ \-\-runtime \fIprocess|docker|podman|kubernetes\fR]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\- \fIARGS...\fR ]
.RE
.I PROGRAM
is an absolute path or a name on
.BR PATH ;
the timeout defaults to 120 seconds.
.B acp run\-status \-\-run\-id \fIID\fR
shows a tracked dispatch run's status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update
Skip the automatic update check.  By default
.B loom
checks GitHub for a newer release at most once per 24 hours (marker
file
.BR ~/.loom/.cache/version_check )
and prints a notice to stderr when one is available.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the Loom version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOOM_AGENTS_DIR
The Loom data directory used by
.B loomd
and passed to spawned agent tools (default
.BR ~/.loom/ ).
.TP
.B LOOM_DIR
The host Loom data directory mounted read\-only into container
runtimes (docker/podman/kubernetes) so containerized agents can see
the ecosystem.
.TP
.B LOOM_NO_EXTEND
Set to
.B 1
to skip the
.B extends
config layer for this invocation.
.TP
.B LOOM_NO_REMOTE
Set to
.B 1
to skip the cached remote config layer for this invocation.
.TP
.B LOOM_TASK_ID ", " LOOM_TASK_PHASE ", " LOOM_TASK_TITLE ", " LOOM_TASK_DESCRIPTION
Set for agents dispatched by
.B "workflow dispatch" .
.TP
.B LOOM_PHASE ", " LOOM_AGENT ", " LOOM_EXIT_CODE
Set during
.B PostPhase
hook execution (the workflow phase and agent that just exited).
.TP
.B LOOM_EXPECTED_RESULT_PATH
Set during workflow dispatch to the path the agent should write its
phase result file to.
.TP
.B LOOM_PRIOR_PHASE_RESULT
Set during workflow dispatch to the JSON of the most recent phase
result, when one exists.
.TP
.B LOOM_PRIOR_SESSIONS
Set during workflow dispatch to the comma\-separated session ids of
prior phases.
.TP
.B LOOM_ROUTING_PROVIDER
Default LLM provider for
.B "sessions resume"
(flag, then this variable, then
.B routing.default_provider
in config).
.TP
.B LOOM_SKILLS_DIR ", " LOOM_MCP_DIR ", " LOOM_SESSIONS_DIR
Set for launched agent tools when skills, MCP, or session sharing is
enabled for them.
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
Default token for GitHub API calls
.RB ( "issues" ,
.B "workflow create \-\-from\-issue" ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.loom/
The shared ecosystem directory.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/config.toml
Main configuration.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/config/
Optional per\-subsystem configuration overlays
(\fBrouting.toml\fR, \fBmcp.toml\fR, \fBhooks.toml\fR, \fBacp.toml\fR).
.TP
.B ~/.loom/loomd.sock
The daemon's Unix domain IPC socket.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/.loom\-events
The ZeroMQ socket used to broadcast cross\-process events
(cross\-process feature).
.TP
.B ~/.loom/skills/
Shared skills, the SQLite registry
.BR skills.db ,
and the
.B skills.lock
lock file.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/mcp/
MCP server configurations.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/mcp_registry.db
SQLite registry of installed MCP servers.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/sessions/
Session exports (JSONL) and portable bundles under
.BR sessions/exports/ .
.TP
.B ~/.loom/auth/
Encrypted credential vault and audit logs.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/hooks/
Hook configuration files and scripts.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/tools/
Per\-tool TOML registration files.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/workflow/tasks/
Workflow task manifests and per\-phase result files
.RB ( {task_id}.{phase}.result.json ).
.TP
.B ~/.loom/worktrees/
Per\-task git worktrees created by
.B "workflow create" .
.TP
.B ~/.loom/knowledge/graph.db
The SQLite knowledge graph (entities, relationships, FTS5).
.TP
.B ~/.loom/runs/
ACP dispatch run tracking.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/.cache/
Snapshot cache, the remote config cache
.BR remote_config/ ,
.BR loomd.pid ,
and the
.B version_check
marker.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The CLI exits 0 on success and non\-zero on error.  When
.B "workflow dispatch"
is invoked with
.BR \-\-auto\-advance ,
the first non\-zero agent exit code propagates as the CLI exit code
and aborts the phase chain.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loomd (1)
